## Building a Cafe Menu

A menu item has a name, price, and size. The size is an enum so only valid options are used.

### The Size Enum

```xiom
enum Size {
  Small,
  Medium,
  Large,
}
```

### The MenuItem Struct

```xiom
type MenuItem = {
  name: Str;
  price: Float64;
  size: Size;
}
```

### Creating Menu Items

```xiom
let latte = MenuItem{
  name: "Latte";
  price: 4.50;
  size: Size.Medium;
};

let espresso = MenuItem{
  name: "Espresso";
  price: 2.75;
  size: Size.Small;
};
```

### Formatting the Price

A function that produces a readable string from a MenuItem:

```xiom
fn format_price(item: MenuItem) -> Str {
  return item.name + " ($" + item.price + ")";
}
```

### Using Size in Logic

Check the size to adjust pricing:

```xiom
fn price_for_size(item: MenuItem, desired: Size) -> Float64 {
  let base = item.price;
  if desired == Size.Large {
    return base * 1.5;
  }
  if desired == Size.Small {
    return base * 0.8;
  }
  return base;
}
```

